              "id": "falco_output_syntax",
              "name": "FalcoOutputSyntax",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The output template does not format: a `%` at the end, a length with no field, or a token that is no field or transformer."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Falco condition does not parse."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# falco_parse_error\n\nThe Falco condition does not parse.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [Falco condition reference](https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "falco_parse_error\n\nThe Falco condition does not parse.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The Falco condition reference (https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#falco_parse_error",
              "id": "falco_parse_error",
              "name": "FalcoParseError",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The Falco condition does not parse."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A `regex` check a plain operator (`=`, `contains`, `startswith`, `endswith`) could make, which libsinsp warns about: regex is the slowest check."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# falco_regex_simple\n\nA `regex` check a plain operator (`=`, `contains`, `startswith`, `endswith`) could make, which libsinsp warns about: regex is the slowest check.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [Falco condition reference](https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "falco_regex_simple\n\nA regex check a plain operator (=, contains, startswith, endswith) could make, which libsinsp warns about: regex is the slowest check.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The Falco condition reference (https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#falco_regex_simple",
              "id": "falco_regex_simple",
              "name": "FalcoRegexSimple",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A `regex` check a plain operator (`=`, `contains`, `startswith`, `endswith`) could make, which libsinsp warns about: regex is the slowest check."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A field cannot be compared with another field here (`val(...)` or a transformer on the right): not with `pmatch` or `regex`, not on networks, not on fields that refuse it, and only between fields of the same type."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# falco_rhs_field\n\nA field cannot be compared with another field here (`val(...)` or a transformer on the right): not with `pmatch` or `regex`, not on networks, not on fields that refuse it, and only between fields of the same type.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [Falco condition reference](https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "falco_rhs_field\n\nA field cannot be compared with another field here (val(...) or a transformer on the right): not with pmatch or regex, not on networks, not on fields that refuse it, and only between fields of the same type.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The Falco condition reference (https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
