            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The name is not a macro of the block or of the Falco default rules; the tenant may define it, as Sysdig does for its managed macros."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# falco_unknown_macro\n\nThe name is not a macro of the block or of the Falco default rules; the tenant may define it, as Sysdig does for its managed macros.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [Falco condition reference](https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "falco_unknown_macro\n\nThe name is not a macro of the block or of the Falco default rules; the tenant may define it, as Sysdig does for its managed macros.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The Falco condition reference (https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#falco_unknown_macro",
              "id": "falco_unknown_macro",
              "name": "FalcoUnknownMacro",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The name is not a macro of the block or of the Falco default rules; the tenant may define it, as Sysdig does for its managed macros."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A tuning (`append_to_rule`) names a rule the Falco default rules do not define: Falco refuses the append, and on Sysdig the tenant must have that rule."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# falco_unknown_rule\n\nA tuning (`append_to_rule`) names a rule the Falco default rules do not define: Falco refuses the append, and on Sysdig the tenant must have that rule.\n\nReported by the analysis engine on the Sysdig block's `append_to_rule`, as a warning: `opentide lint` (its `queries` check) shows it. Since UC-2.6 an editor running `opentide lsp start` does not: it publishes what `opentide validate` reports on the object, and the block's advisories are lint's.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [Falco condition reference](https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "falco_unknown_rule\n\nA tuning (append_to_rule) names a rule the Falco default rules do not define: Falco refuses the append, and on Sysdig the tenant must have that rule.\n\nReported by the analysis engine on the Sysdig block's append_to_rule, as a warning: opentide lint (its queries check) shows it. Since UC-2.6 an editor running opentide lsp start does not: it publishes what opentide validate reports on the object, and the block's advisories are lint's.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The Falco condition reference (https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#falco_unknown_rule",
              "id": "falco_unknown_rule",
              "name": "FalcoUnknownRule",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A tuning (`append_to_rule`) names a rule the Falco default rules do not define: Falco refuses the append, and on Sysdig the tenant must have that rule."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The event source is not one Falco or its published plugins define, so its fields are not checked."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# falco_unknown_source\n\nThe event source is not one Falco or its published plugins define, so its fields are not checked.\n\nReported by the analysis engine on the Sysdig block's `source`, as a warning, with the condition's findings (its fields go unchecked): `opentide lint` (its `queries` check) and an editor running `opentide lsp start` show it; `opentide validate` does not fail on it.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [Falco condition reference](https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "falco_unknown_source\n\nThe event source is not one Falco or its published plugins define, so its fields are not checked.\n\nReported by the analysis engine on the Sysdig block's source, as a warning, with the condition's findings (its fields go unchecked): opentide lint (its queries check) and an editor running opentide lsp start show it; opentide validate does not fail on it.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The Falco condition reference (https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#falco_unknown_source",
              "id": "falco_unknown_source",
              "name": "FalcoUnknownSource",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The event source is not one Falco or its published plugins define, so its fields are not checked."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A `ka.` or `jevt.` field compared with `<NA>`, which Falco warns about: the field may hold that text."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# falco_unsafe_na_check\n\nA `ka.` or `jevt.` field compared with `<NA>`, which Falco warns about: the field may hold that text.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [Falco condition reference](https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "falco_unsafe_na_check\n\nA ka. or jevt. field compared with <NA>, which Falco warns about: the field may hold that text.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The Falco condition reference (https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#falco_unsafe_na_check",
              "id": "falco_unsafe_na_check",
              "name": "FalcoUnsafeNaCheck",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A `ka.` or `jevt.` field compared with `<NA>`, which Falco warns about: the field may hold that text."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The value cannot be parsed as the field's type (a number, `true` or `false`, an IP address or network, a hex string for `bcontains`); Falco refuses to load the rule."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# falco_value_type\n\nThe value cannot be parsed as the field's type (a number, `true` or `false`, an IP address or network, a hex string for `bcontains`); Falco refuses to load the rule.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [Falco condition reference](https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "falco_value_type\n\nThe value cannot be parsed as the field's type (a number, true or false, an IP address or network, a hex string for bcontains); Falco refuses to load the rule.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a Falco condition query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The Falco condition reference (https://falco.org/docs/concepts/rules/conditions/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#falco_value_type",
              "id": "falco_value_type",
              "name": "FalcoValueType",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The value cannot be parsed as the field's type (a number, `true` or `false`, an IP address or network, a hex string for `bcontains`); Falco refuses to load the rule."
              }
