            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The YARA signature has no rule, or only private or global rules."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yara_empty_signature\n\nThe YARA signature has no rule, or only private or global rules.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA rule reference](https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yara_empty_signature\n\nThe YARA signature has no rule, or only private or global rules.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA rule reference (https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yara_empty_signature",
              "id": "yara_empty_signature",
              "name": "YaraEmptySignature",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The YARA signature has no rule, or only private or global rules."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "entrypoint is deprecated in libyara and refused by YARA-X (yara_undefined_identifier); use pe.entry_point or elf.entry_point."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yara_entrypoint_deprecated\n\nentrypoint is deprecated in libyara and refused by YARA-X (yara_undefined_identifier); use pe.entry_point or elf.entry_point.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query, as a warning that names the replacement, together with the error `yara_undefined_identifier` at the same place: YARA-X refuses `entrypoint`, so `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query` fail on the rule; `opentide lint` (its `queries` check) and an editor running `opentide lsp start` show both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide lint --check queries\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA rule reference](https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yara_entrypoint_deprecated\n\nentrypoint is deprecated in libyara and refused by YARA-X (yara_undefined_identifier); use pe.entry_point or elf.entry_point.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query, as a warning that names the replacement, together with the error yara_undefined_identifier at the same place: YARA-X refuses entrypoint, so opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query fail on the rule; opentide lint (its queries check) and an editor running opentide lsp start show both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide lint --check queries\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA rule reference (https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yara_entrypoint_deprecated",
              "id": "yara_entrypoint_deprecated",
              "name": "YaraEntrypointDeprecated",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "entrypoint is deprecated in libyara and refused by YARA-X (yara_undefined_identifier); use pe.entry_point or elf.entry_point."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA hex string is invalid: an odd number of nibbles, a bad jump, or unbalanced alternatives."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yara_hex_string\n\nA YARA hex string is invalid: an odd number of nibbles, a bad jump, or unbalanced alternatives.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA rule reference](https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yara_hex_string\n\nA YARA hex string is invalid: an odd number of nibbles, a bad jump, or unbalanced alternatives.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA rule reference (https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yara_hex_string",
              "id": "yara_hex_string",
              "name": "YaraHexString",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA hex string is invalid: an odd number of nibbles, a bad jump, or unbalanced alternatives."
