            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA signature uses an include directive, which no platform resolves: each API takes one text with no file system behind it."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yara_include\n\nA YARA signature uses an include directive, which no platform resolves: each API takes one text with no file system behind it.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA rule reference](https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yara_include\n\nA YARA signature uses an include directive, which no platform resolves: each API takes one text with no file system behind it.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA rule reference (https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yara_include",
              "id": "yara_include",
              "name": "YaraInclude",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA signature uses an include directive, which no platform resolves: each API takes one text with no file system behind it."
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A HarfangLab YARA rule has no meta `context`, which the HarfangLab profile recommends on every rule that is not private."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yara_meta_missing\n\nA HarfangLab YARA rule has no meta `context`, which the HarfangLab profile recommends on every rule that is not private.\n\nSeverity: warning. Reported by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check) on a HarfangLab rule (`harfanglab`). In the signature form, a rule that is not `private` has no `meta:` section, or one without `context`. `opentide validate` does not fail on it. Deploy sends the signature verbatim and adds no meta, so the agent receives the rule without saying where to scan. In the decomposed form, an empty `meta.context: []` is the same finding: deploy then writes the rule with no `context` line.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  harfanglab:\n    yara:\n      signature: |\n        rule Cmd_String {\n          strings:\n            $a = \"cmd.exe\" ascii\n          condition:\n            $a\n        }\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nAdd a `meta:` section with `context` to the rule (`file`, `memory`, or `file,memory`), then run `opentide lint --check queries` again. A `private` helper rule needs none.\n\n```yaml\n        rule Cmd_String {\n          meta:\n            context = \"file\"\n          strings:\n            $a = \"cmd.exe\" ascii\n          condition:\n            $a\n        }\n```\n",
                "text": "yara_meta_missing\n\nA HarfangLab YARA rule has no meta context, which the HarfangLab profile recommends on every rule that is not private.\n\nSeverity: warning. Reported by opentide lint (its queries check) on a HarfangLab rule (harfanglab). In the signature form, a rule that is not private has no meta: section, or one without context. opentide validate does not fail on it. Deploy sends the signature verbatim and adds no meta, so the agent receives the rule without saying where to scan. In the decomposed form, an empty meta.context: [] is the same finding: deploy then writes the rule with no context line.\n\nExample\n\nconfigurations:\n  harfanglab:\n    yara:\n      signature: |\n        rule Cmd_String {\n          strings:\n            $a = \"cmd.exe\" ascii\n          condition:\n            $a\n        }\n\nHow to fix\n\nAdd a meta: section with context to the rule (file, memory, or file,memory), then run opentide lint --check queries again. A private helper rule needs none.\n\n        rule Cmd_String {\n          meta:\n            context = \"file\"\n          strings:\n            $a = \"cmd.exe\" ascii\n          condition:\n            $a\n        }"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yara_meta_missing",
              "id": "yara_meta_missing",
              "name": "YaraMetaMissing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A HarfangLab YARA rule has no meta `context`, which the HarfangLab profile recommends on every rule that is not private."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA module field or function is used without importing its module."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yara_module_not_imported\n\nA YARA module field or function is used without importing its module.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA rule reference](https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yara_module_not_imported\n\nA YARA module field or function is used without importing its module.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA rule reference (https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yara_module_not_imported",
              "id": "yara_module_not_imported",
              "name": "YaraModuleNotImported",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA module field or function is used without importing its module."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The YARA module is known but not confirmed on the platform's agents."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yara_module_unconfirmed\n\nThe YARA module is known but not confirmed on the platform's agents.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query, always as a warning: the platform takes the rule, so `opentide validate` does not fail on it, and `opentide lint` (its `queries` check) and an editor running `opentide lsp start` show it.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide lint --check queries\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA rule reference](https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yara_module_unconfirmed\n\nThe YARA module is known but not confirmed on the platform's agents.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA rule query, at the place in the query, always as a warning: the platform takes the rule, so opentide validate does not fail on it, and opentide lint (its queries check) and an editor running opentide lsp start show it.\n\nExample\n\nopentide lint --check queries\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA rule reference (https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yara_module_unconfirmed",
              "id": "yara_module_unconfirmed",
              "name": "YaraModuleUnconfirmed",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The YARA module is known but not confirmed on the platform's agents."
              }
            },
