            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The regular expression starts with `.*` without an anchor: RE2 matches anywhere already, and the prefix only costs time."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_leading_wildcard_regex\n\nThe regular expression starts with `.*` without an anchor: RE2 matches anywhere already, and the prefix only costs time.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA-L 2.0 reference](https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yaral_leading_wildcard_regex\n\nThe regular expression starts with .* without an anchor: RE2 matches anywhere already, and the prefix only costs time.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA-L 2.0 reference (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_leading_wildcard_regex",
              "id": "yaral_leading_wildcard_regex",
              "name": "YaralLeadingWildcardRegex",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The regular expression starts with `.*` without an anchor: RE2 matches anywhere already, and the prefix only costs time."
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L `match` is not a `YaraLMatch` object."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_match_shape\n\nA YARA-L `match` is not a `YaraLMatch` object.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by `opentide validate` (its `schema` check) on a `configurations.google_secops` block (yara-l-1.0). `match` takes `group_by` (a non-empty list of distinct `$placeholders`), `window`, `type` (`hop`, `tumbling` or `sliding`), and, for `sliding` only, `pivot` (an `$event`) and `direction` (`before` or `after`). The finding is on `match` or on the field at fault.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    match:\n      group_by: [$user]\n      window: 5m\n      type: sliding\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nAdd the event the sliding window is anchored on and its direction, or use a hop window:\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    match:\n      group_by: [$user]\n      window: 5m\n      type: sliding\n      pivot: $login\n      direction: after\n```\n",
                "text": "yaral_match_shape\n\nA YARA-L match is not a YaraLMatch object.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by opentide validate (its schema check) on a configurations.google_secops block (yara-l-1.0). match takes group_by (a non-empty list of distinct $placeholders), window, type (hop, tumbling or sliding), and, for sliding only, pivot (an $event) and direction (before or after). The finding is on match or on the field at fault.\n\nExample\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    match:\n      group_by: [$user]\n      window: 5m\n      type: sliding\n\nHow to fix\n\nAdd the event the sliding window is anchored on and its direction, or use a hop window:\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    match:\n      group_by: [$user]\n      window: 5m\n      type: sliding\n      pivot: $login\n      direction: after"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_match_shape",
              "id": "yaral_match_shape",
              "name": "YaralMatchShape",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L `match` is not a `YaraLMatch` object."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A `match` name is not a placeholder bound in `events`."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_match_variable\n\nA `match` name is not a placeholder bound in `events`.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA-L 2.0 reference](https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yaral_match_variable\n\nA match name is not a placeholder bound in events.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA-L 2.0 reference (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_match_variable",
              "id": "yaral_match_variable",
              "name": "YaralMatchVariable",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A `match` name is not a placeholder bound in `events`."
              }
