            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L keyword is used as a rule name, meta key or variable, or a variable is named `$window_start` or `$window_end`."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_reserved_identifier\n\nA YARA-L keyword is used as a rule name, meta key or variable, or a variable is named `$window_start` or `$window_end`.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA-L 2.0 reference](https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yaral_reserved_identifier\n\nA YARA-L keyword is used as a rule name, meta key or variable, or a variable is named $window_start or $window_end.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA-L 2.0 reference (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_reserved_identifier",
              "id": "yaral_reserved_identifier",
              "name": "YaralReservedIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L keyword is used as a rule name, meta key or variable, or a variable is named `$window_start` or `$window_end`."
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section key is a YAML alias instead of its own text."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_section_alias\n\nA YARA-L section key is a YAML alias instead of its own text.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by `opentide validate` (its `schema` check) on a `configurations.google_secops` block (yara-l-1.0). What a block deploys must be readable in the block: an alias makes a change to the anchored text, under any other key, change the deployed rule too. The YAML loader cannot tell an alias from text written in place, so `opentide validate` reads the file's node graph.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\ndescription: &shared |\n  $e\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: *shared\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nWrite the section text under its key with a block scalar (`|`).\n",
                "text": "yaral_section_alias\n\nA YARA-L section key is a YAML alias instead of its own text.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by opentide validate (its schema check) on a configurations.google_secops block (yara-l-1.0). What a block deploys must be readable in the block: an alias makes a change to the anchored text, under any other key, change the deployed rule too. The YAML loader cannot tell an alias from text written in place, so opentide validate reads the file's node graph.\n\nExample\n\ndescription: &shared |\n  $e\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: *shared\n\nHow to fix\n\nWrite the section text under its key with a block scalar (|)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_section_alias",
              "id": "yaral_section_alias",
              "name": "YaralSectionAlias",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section key is a YAML alias instead of its own text."
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section key is present with no text."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_section_empty\n\nA YARA-L section key is present with no text.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by `opentide validate` (its `schema` check) on a `configurations.google_secops` block (yara-l-1.0). The key loaded as YAML `null` or blank text, or as a YAML list or mapping instead of text. A plain YAML scalar that starts with `#` is a YAML comment, so `condition: #fail > 3` loads as null.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: #e > 5\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nWrite each section as a block scalar (`|`), which YAML keeps verbatim:\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: |\n      #e > 5\n```\n",
                "text": "yaral_section_empty\n\nA YARA-L section key is present with no text.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by opentide validate (its schema check) on a configurations.google_secops block (yara-l-1.0). The key loaded as YAML null or blank text, or as a YAML list or mapping instead of text. A plain YAML scalar that starts with # is a YAML comment, so condition: #fail > 3 loads as null.\n\nExample\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: #e > 5\n\nHow to fix\n\nWrite each section as a block scalar (|), which YAML keeps verbatim:\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: |\n      #e > 5"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_section_empty",
              "id": "yaral_section_empty",
              "name": "YaralSectionEmpty",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section key is present with no text."
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section text holds a section label, a `rule` header or a rule's braces."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_section_header\n\nA YARA-L section text holds a section label, a `rule` header or a rule's braces.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by `opentide validate` (its `schema` check) on a `configurations.google_secops` block (yara-l-1.0). Each section is its own key, and deploy writes the `rule <name> {` header, the `meta` section and the labels itself. A label or a header inside a comment or a string does not count.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      rule office_powershell {\n        events:\n          $e.metadata.event_type = \"PROCESS_LAUNCH\"\n        condition:\n          $e\n      }\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nMove each section's lines under its own key and drop the header, `meta` and braces:\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      $e.metadata.event_type = \"PROCESS_LAUNCH\"\n    condition: |\n      $e\n```\n",
                "text": "yaral_section_header\n\nA YARA-L section text holds a section label, a rule header or a rule's braces.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by opentide validate (its schema check) on a configurations.google_secops block (yara-l-1.0). Each section is its own key, and deploy writes the rule <name> { header, the meta section and the labels itself. A label or a header inside a comment or a string does not count.\n\nExample\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      rule office_powershell {\n        events:\n          $e.metadata.event_type = \"PROCESS_LAUNCH\"\n        condition:\n          $e\n      }\n\nHow to fix\n\nMove each section's lines under its own key and drop the header, meta and braces:\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      $e.metadata.event_type = \"PROCESS_LAUNCH\"\n    condition: |\n      $e"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_section_header",
              "id": "yaral_section_header",
              "name": "YaralSectionHeader",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section text holds a section label, a `rule` header or a rule's braces."
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L rule has no `events` or no `condition` section."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_section_missing\n\nA YARA-L rule has no `events` or no `condition` section.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by `opentide validate` (its `schema` check) on a `configurations.google_secops` block (yara-l-1.0). A rule needs both: `events` names what to match, `condition` when it fires. The finding is on the missing key.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      $e.metadata.event_type = \"NETWORK_DNS\"\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nAdd the missing key, as a block scalar:\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: |\n      $e\n```\n",
                "text": "yaral_section_missing\n\nA YARA-L rule has no events or no condition section.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by opentide validate (its schema check) on a configurations.google_secops block (yara-l-1.0). A rule needs both: events names what to match, condition when it fires. The finding is on the missing key.\n\nExample\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      $e.metadata.event_type = \"NETWORK_DNS\"\n\nHow to fix\n\nAdd the missing key, as a block scalar:\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: |\n      $e"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_section_missing",
              "id": "yaral_section_missing",
              "name": "YaralSectionMissing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L rule has no `events` or no `condition` section."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section is repeated or out of order (meta, setup, events, match, outcome, condition, options, export)."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_section_order\n\nA YARA-L section is repeated or out of order (meta, setup, events, match, outcome, condition, options, export).\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA-L 2.0 reference](https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yaral_section_order\n\nA YARA-L section is repeated or out of order (meta, setup, events, match, outcome, condition, options, export).\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA-L 2.0 reference (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_section_order",
              "id": "yaral_section_order",
              "name": "YaralSectionOrder",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section is repeated or out of order (meta, setup, events, match, outcome, condition, options, export)."
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The section is not part of this profile: `dedup`, `order`, `limit`, `select` and `unselect` are search sections; `meta`, `setup` and `options` are rule sections."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# yaral_section_unavailable\n\nThe section is not part of this profile: `dedup`, `order`, `limit`, `select` and `unselect` are search sections; `meta`, `setup` and `options` are rule sections.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by `opentide validate` (its `queries` check) and `opentide validate query`; as a warning or a note, style, by `opentide lint` (its `queries` check). An editor running `opentide lsp start` shows both.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide validate query\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run `opentide validate query` (`--file` for one rule or query file) or `opentide lint --check queries` again. The [YARA-L 2.0 reference](https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against.\n",
                "text": "yaral_section_unavailable\n\nThe section is not part of this profile: dedup, order, limit, select and unselect are search sections; meta, setup and options are rule sections.\n\nReported by the analysis engine in a YARA-L 2.0 query, at the place in the query: as an error, a query the platform would reject, by opentide validate (its queries check) and opentide validate query; as a warning or a note, style, by opentide lint (its queries check). An editor running opentide lsp start shows both.\n\nExample\n\nopentide validate query\n\nHow to fix\n\nChange the query where the frame points, then run opentide validate query (--file for one rule or query file) or opentide lint --check queries again. The YARA-L 2.0 reference (https://cloud.google.com/chronicle/docs/detection/yara-l-2-0-syntax) describes the syntax and the commands the engine checks against."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_section_unavailable",
              "id": "yaral_section_unavailable",
              "name": "YaralSectionUnavailable",
              "shortDescription": {
